---

<BlogPostLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  seoTitle={seoTitle}
  seoDescription={seoDescription}
  canonical={canonical}
  category="career-options"
  publishedAt={publishedDateISO}
  publishedLabel={publishedDateLabel}
  authorName={authorName}
  authorUrl={authorUrl}
  authorRole={authorRole}
  jsonLdExtras={[faqJsonLd]}
>
  <p class="lead-para">
    <strong>Geography career options in India go well past teaching and UPSC.</strong> The real
    list has nine routes: GIS and spatial data, location analytics for business, environment and
    climate consulting, urban planning, disaster management, remote sensing, surveying, NET
    teaching and civil services. Which ones are open to you depends on three things: whether you
    studied maths, whether you add one spatial skill, and whether you can show work. Those
    decisions shape your income ceiling and how early you reach financial freedom more than the
    BA or BSc label does.
  </p>

  <div class="key-takeaways">
    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Lead with the skills that sell as projects.</strong> GIS analytics and business location analytics can grow into consulting. Civil services, NET, Survey of India and ISRO posts are real, but they are rank-gated, so we rate them Not so scalable and you need a second plan.</li>
      <li><strong>Check the entry rule before you plan years around a post.</strong> Survey of India's published rules ask for maths. NRSC's 2024 project posts asked for a remote sensing and GIS master's, not a geography degree alone.</li>
      <li><strong>Next step:</strong> pick two routes, run them through The 4-Checkpoint Protocol below, and build one finished map project. That one project is the start of a high-income skill portfolio.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p>
    This guide sits inside our wider set of
    <a href="/blog/career-options/">career options for every stream and degree</a>. If you also
    like the environmental side of geography, compare it with
    <a href="/blog/career-options/environmental-science-career-options/">environmental science career options</a>.
    If you are weighing a humanities route more broadly, read
    <a href="/blog/career-options/career-options-in-arts/">career options in arts</a>.
  </p>

